+
+The same object/value boundary applies to `c_ir_emit_compound_assignment`:
+use the unqualified computation type for volatile as well as atomic objects,
+while retaining the qualified place for loads/stores and the existing atomic
+read-modify-write path. `basic_c_qualified_compound.c` and
+`c_test_qualified_compound_values` guard exact binary operand/result types,
+volatile accesses, and canonical preparation in both frontend forms. The
+qualified-aggregate differential case also exercises a nested volatile pointer.
